I added `blockers()` to `Handover`, placed just before `reading()`. It returns the codes of items that are `must` and in state `todo` or `fault`, from the `out` list while `checking` and the `back` list while `returned`, and an empty list in any other phase. It builds a new array and changes nothing in the handover. I couldn't run or compile anything, so it is untested.
